  "body": "Branch base: upstream/main 2b6e03f2.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_bore.rs`, the `Entry3D::Ramp` arm (no entry ramp angle set):\n  - The single chord stays only when it is not steeper than the links' ramp angle (3 deg by default).\n  - On a closed ring, the chord has no run. In that case, or when the chord is steeper, the ramp zig-zags along the lead-in and the ring at that angle. It uses the same `plan_zig_capped` and `push_zig` as the entry-angle arm.\n  - When the path is too short for the angle, the descent substitutes by name (\"the lead-in and ring are too short to ramp at the angle\"). This is an axial dive at the plunge feed with an `entry:` note.\n  - A blocked chord substitutes by name, as before.\n  - Side Outside does not change.\n- New helpers in the same file: `level_angle`, `within_angle`, `zig_onto`. The entry-angle arm now uses `zig_onto` too. Its output does not change.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1664-contour-inside-ramp.md`.\n\n## Pins\n\nNew suite `crates/motion/tests/contour_inside_ramp.rs`:\n- `a_bore_side_ramp_entry_contour_never_descends_steeper_than_its_ramp_angle`: the issue repro, climb and conventional. Each descending feed move is at most 3 deg, or an axial move at the plunge feed with an `entry:` note. This ring has room, so there is no dive.\n- `a_bore_side_ring_too_short_to_ramp_dives_by_name_at_the_plunge_feed`: `ramp_max_len` 0.1. Each level dives by name at the plunge feed.\n\n## Mutation checks\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| upstream/main `contour_bore.rs` (today's code) | both pins red |\n| `within_angle` always true (a chord with no run is accepted) | both red |\n| `level_angle` returns 10 deg | both red |\n| a short path feeds straight down at the cutting feed, no note | the short-ring pin red |\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (motion lib, `contour_inside_ramp`, `entry_approach`, `one_descent`).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion` (all suites): green.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app` (all suites, golden CL and posts included): green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens\n\nNo golden file moved. No committed golden has a bore-side Contour with a Ramp entry. Posted G-code changes only for that case. This is on the safety floor.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- UI suites (no UI change).\n- A Windows run.\n\n## Dependency\n\nNo dependency on #1663. This fix does not use `descent::plan_arm`, because the contour pushes its moves directly. The two PRs do not touch the same files. They can merge in either order.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Contour on the inside with a Ramp entry now descends at the ramp angle (zig-zag along the ring), or dives by name at the plunge feed; it no longer feeds straight down at the cutting feed (#1664).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nFixes #1664\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
